※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4468

※ Two loops one inside the other sharing a label would leave no way to name the
※ outer one from inside the inner, a name meaning the nearest thing it could
※ mean.  A label exists to say which loop is meant, and one that hides another
※ says less than it appears to.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    while §counting true:
        while §counting true:
            break §counting
    0u6
